UID:http://calagator.org/events/1250482543
DESCRIPTION:This presentation introduces D3.js as a powerful tool for tra
 nsforming complex data into clear\, meaningful visual stories which non-
 technical audiences can understand and use. It explains what D3.js is\, 
 how it works with web technologies and why visualization is essential fo
 r revealing patterns and insights raw data alone cannot show.&#13\;\n&#1
 3\;\nThis talk emphasizes designing visualizations with the audience in 
 mind while also covering core D3 concepts such as data binding\, scales\
 , layouts and interactive graphics. Through examples\, case studies\, de
 sign principles and practical tips\, this presentation demonstrates how 
 builders can use D3.js to communicate ideas effectively and empower peop
 le to discover insights from data.\n\nTags: portland design thinkers\, d
 ata visualizations\, UX research\, problem solving\, collaboration\, inn
 ovation\n\nImported from: http://calagator.org/events/1250482543
URL:https://www.meetup.com/portland-design-thinkers/events/314420080/
SUMMARY:Building D3.js Visualizations For Non-Technical Audiences
LOCATION:Virtual: false
SEQUENCE:1
END:VEVENT
